  "description": "We are proposing to create a treehouse in the outdoor area of Ambler Children’s Centre, which we call ‘the Forest’. Although we are fortunate to have the space, it is in need of renovation to ensure it continues to meet the needs of our pupils and meet health and safety requirements. \n\nThe treehouse will provide a unique, elevated space that encourages exploration, curiosity, and creativity. It is designed to blend with the natural environment and will become a focal point for outdoor learning. The treehouse will support the delivery of the EYFS statutory framework and children’s personal, social, emotional and physical development.\n\nIt will be a standalone structure constructed using pressure treated timber, supported by 100mm poles concreted into the ground. The roof will be clad with cedar shingles to blend with the existing natural environment. The design comprises an elevated decked platform with the treehouse in one corner and a rope bridge to a smaller wooden platform. The smaller platform will have a cargo net to ground level and the larger decking area is accessed by stairs. \n\nPlease refer to section 7 supplementary information for details of proposed location and dimensions of treehouse.",
